    "result_text": "The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS). Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` field, formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year.\n\nSince the value is fully derived from the owner's own already-stored fields (`customerCode` + `registrationDate`), I implemented it the same way the existing derived, read-only fields `displayName` and `initials` are done \u2014 as a computed mapping rather than a persisted column or extra pipeline step (which would have required schema migrations across all four DBs):\n\n- **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` string property to the `Owner` schema (so `OwnerDto` is generated with the field).\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression:\n  ```\n  owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100)\n  ```\n  The `%02d` zero-pads so e.g. year 2007 \u2192 `07`, matching the spec example `SMI-0007-M26`.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreMembershipNumberFormat` passes and the full `./mvnw test` suite is green.",
